                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 332,
                "end_index": 583,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Positive Result (Two lines, a plus sign, or \"Pregnant\"):** If you see a second line\u2014even if it is **very faint**\u2014it is almost certainly a positive result, as long as it appeared within the recommended reading window (usually 3 to 10 minutes)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 586,
                "end_index": 762,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Negative Result (One line, a minus sign, or \"Not Pregnant\"):** This means the test did not detect the pregnancy hormone, hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin), in your urine"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 785,
                "end_index": 921,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Evaporation Line:** A true faint positive line will have color (usually pink or blue) and appear within the test's designated time frame"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 923,
                "end_index": 1082,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "An **evaporation line** is a faint, colorless, or grayish line that appears *after* the reading window has closed, caused by the urine drying on the test strip"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1143,
                "end_index": 1378,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "When to Test for the Most Accurate Results\n*   **Wait for a missed period:** While some \"early detection\" tests claim to work sooner, home pregnancy tests are over 99% accurate when taken on or after the first day of your missed period"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1380,
                "end_index": 1442,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Testing too early is the most common cause of a false negative"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1444,
                "end_index": 1531,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Use first morning urine:** Your urine is most concentrated when you first wake up"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1533,
                "end_index": 1647,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Testing first thing in the morning ensures that hCG levels, if present, are at their highest and easiest to detect"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1657,
                "end_index": 1755,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Understanding Inaccurate Results\nWhile home pregnancy tests are highly reliable, errors can happen"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1859,
                "end_index": 1922,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Your body has not yet produced enough hCG to trigger a positive"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1949,
                "end_index": 2050,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Drinking too much water or other fluids right before taking the test can dilute the hCG in your urine"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2056,
                "end_index": 2223,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   *The \"Hook Effect\" (Rare):* In rare cases, if you are more than a few weeks pregnant, extremely high levels of hCG can overwhelm the test, causing a false negative"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2342,
                "end_index": 2470,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "If you have recently experienced a miscarriage, abortion, or chemical pregnancy, hCG can remain in your system for several weeks"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2505,
                "end_index": 2615,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "If you are undergoing fertility treatments and received an hCG \"trigger shot,\" this can cause a false positive"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2617,
                "end_index": 2704,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "(Most other medications, like antibiotics or birth control, do not affect test results)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2744,
                "end_index": 2845,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Rare conditions, such as ovarian cysts or hormone-secreting tumors, can occasionally raise hCG levels"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2878,
                "end_index": 3034,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### If Your Test is Positive:\n*   **Confirm with a doctor:** Schedule an appointment with an obstetrician/gynecologist (OB-GYN) or your primary care doctor"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                12,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3036,
                "end_index": 3161,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "They can perform a clinical blood test and schedule an ultrasound to confirm the pregnancy and ensure it is developing safely"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3554,
                "end_index": 3750,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### If Your Test is Negative (but your period is still late):\n*   **Wait and retest:** If your period still hasn\u2019t arrived, wait 3 to 4 days and take another test using your first morning urine"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3753,
                "end_index": 3903,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Consult a doctor:** If the second test is also negative and you still do not have your period, make an appointment with your healthcare provider"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3905,
                "end_index": 4072,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Other factors\u2014such as extreme stress, excessive exercise, sudden weight changes, thyroid issues, or polycystic ovary syndrome (PCOS)\u2014can cause you to miss a period"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 4075,
                "end_index": 4316,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*If you are feeling overwhelmed, confused, or unsupported by your results, please reach out to a trusted healthcare provider, counselor, or family planning organization to discuss your feelings and options in a safe, confidential environment"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
